%N A398406 Hexadecimal expansion of the square root of 2.
%H A398406 Adam Reichert, <a href="/A398406/b398406.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A398406 Adam Reichert, <a href="/A398406/a398406.py.txt">Python program</a>
%H A398406 Eric W. Weisstein, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Hexadecimal.html">Hexadecimal</a>
%H A398406 Eric W. Weisstein, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/PythagorassConstant.html">Pythagoras's Constant</a>, MathWorld.
%F A398406 a(1) = 1; for n >= 2, a(n) = 8*A004539(4*n-6) + 4*A004539(4*n-5) + 2*A004539(4*n-4) + A004539(4*n-3).
%e A398406 sqrt(2) = (1.6A09E667F3BCC908B2FB1366EA957D3E3ADEC17512775099D...)_16.
%e A398406 a(12) = 11 because A004539(42), ..., A004539(45) are 1, 0, 1, 1, giving 8*1 + 4*0 + 2*1 + 1 = 11.
%t A398406 First[RealDigits[Sqrt[2], 16, 100]] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Oct 05 2026 *)
